Reverts parts of Helium's helium/core/proxy-extension-downloads.patch and helium/core/spoof-extension-downloader-platform.patch
(GPL-3.0, The Helium Authors) and of ungoogled-chromium's disable-webstore-urls.patch (BSD-3-Clause), which Helium's
series needs for its later patches and so can't be skipped.

Chrome Web Store installs and extension updates go straight to Google again, as they did before Helium: Helium sends
them through its own proxy only after its onboarding consent, which Ray never shows, so every install and update
went to a dummy host and failed.
- the store's update URL is clients2.google.com again, and the item snippet URL chromewebstore.googleapis.com;
- installs, pending installs (sync and external ones included), effective update URLs and the standalone installer
  no longer swap in Helium's proxy URL, and ExtensionUpdater uses the update service again (Omaha attributes, the
  malware kill switch, arrive through it);
- requests say the real platform (os=mac, arch=arm64, prod=chromiumcrx) instead of Windows, so extensions with
  per-platform packages get their Mac build;
- ChromeContentVerifierDelegate::IsFromStore, the store's dedicated process, the extension migrator's update URL,
  https for store updates, the store's daystart and the extension downloader's defaults are Chromium's code again
  (content verification itself stays unenforced, as in unbranded Chromium before Helium).
Helium's no-tracking choice stays: no utm_source on store links. Update pings have no domain (the branding patch).

